 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 544199,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Determine the number of introductions necessary in a room with 500 strangers using the Sum of Degrees Theorem.\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>There are 500 vertices. Each individual must meet 499 other strangers, so there are 499 edges meeting at each vertex. Since there are 500 vertices of degree 499, the sum of degrees is 500(499) = 249,500.</p>\n<p>By the Sum of Degrees Theorem, <span data-math=\"{\\text{the number of edges  =  }}\\frac{{{\\text{sum of degrees}}}}{2} = \\frac{{249,500}}{2} = 124,750{\\text{ introductions}}\"></span>.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "124,750 introductions"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
